ence appears limited to unstructured text without detailed mechanistic explanation [Data: Relationships (5720)]. Separately, 长期卧床病人 (long-term bedridden patients) are contraindicated for 二性霉素B, likely due to heightened susceptibility to systemic toxicity or impaired drug clearance, although the cited evidence excerpt appears unrelated and may reflect data extraction error [Data: Relationships (5438)]. Despite potential documentation issues, these contraindications signal recognized risk categories requiring alternative therapeutic approaches.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"毛地黄 class drugs interact dangerously with 二性霉素B via electrolyte-mediated mechanisms\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The interaction between 二性霉素B and 毛地黄 (digitalis glycosides) represents a high-risk pharmacological combination. 二性霉素B can induce hypokalemia, which in turn sensitizes cardiac tissue to digitalis, increasing the likelihood of severe arrhythmias or 地高辛毒性 [Data: Relationships (27839, 8937)]. Although the direct evidence snippet for the 二性霉素B–毛地黄 interaction lacks explicit mention of potassium, the broader context—supported by the 低血钾症–地高辛毒性 link—strongly implies an electrolyte-mediated pathway. This triad (antifungal → hypokalemia → digitalis toxicity) exemplifies a classic indirect drug interaction with significant clinical implications, necessitating potassium monitoring and cautious co-prescription.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Sequential rather than concurrent use is recommended for vaginal microbiome-targeted therapies\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The relationship between 乳杆菌活菌胶囊 and 克霉唑阴道 emphasizes a sequential treatment paradigm rather than simultaneous administration. Clinical guidance specifies that 克霉唑阴道片 (an antifungal) should be used for a full course first, and only afterward should 乳杆菌活菌胶囊 be introduced to restore vaginal flora [Data: Relationships (27733)]. This approach acknowledges the antagonistic effect of antif